  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business set-aside obligations totaled $400M in FY2027 to date. The program recorded 1,481 awards with an average award size of $270K. Obligations fell 96.0% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show higher historical totals, including $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and $10.1B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in FY2027 to date with $389M of obligations, followed by the Department of Transportation with $2.5M and the Department of Agriculture with $2.4M. Vendors receiving the largest obligations so far include VALIANT CONSTRUCTION LLC with $22.3M and STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC with $19.4M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date at $109M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $53.1M and Temporary Help Services at $32.9M. This snapshot reflects partial fiscal-year totals for FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations were $400M, a marked step down from prior years. Obligations fell 96.0% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, $8.7B in FY25, and $10.1B in FY26, then $400M in FY27. These FY2027 totals are partial, fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominated FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $389M in FY2027 to date, making it the dominant buyer. VALIANT CONSTRUCTION LLC and STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC were the top two vendors with $22.3M and $19.4M respectively. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $109M, followed by Other Computer Related Services with $53.1M and Temporary Help Services with $32.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
